<title>THAILAND: Thailand to ship 18,000 tonnes rice to Iran soon.</title>
<headline>Thailand to ship 18,000 tonnes rice to Iran soon.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand was expected to load 18,000 tonnes of 100 percent grade B rice for shipment to Iran soon, a commerce ministry source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The amount would be the last shipment from an earlier government-to-government contract under which Thailand committed to sell 200,000 tonnes of rice to Iran.</p>
<p>The commerce ministry was awaiting the arrival of ships from Iran, she said.</p>
<p>Although the ministry source declined to reveal the prices, traders said the price was around US$340 per tonne FOB Bangkok.</p>
<p>Thai government and private exporters had exported 283,450 tonnes of rice, mostly 100 percent grade, to Iran between January-August, according to independent surveyor Overseas Merchandise Inspection.</p>
</text>
